# Purpose
Explains how users can start, stop, and check turns using the visible UI,
event log, and gvturn history.

# Key Sections
- Starting turns.
- Checking running turns.
- Power footer actions.
- Stopping or pausing.
- Using eventlog and gvturn history.
- Recovery prompts.

# Dependencies
- `understand-the-status-bar.md`
- `recover-a-failed-turn.md`
- `../concepts/what-is-a-gvturn.md`

# Gotchas
- Keep this user-facing. Do not include private endpoints or service restart
  commands.
- Stopping behavior may vary by UI; advise users to follow visible labels.

# Change History
- 2026-08-03: Added power footer guidance for turn continuation and review.
- 2026-08-03: Created initial turn management guide.
